        "biography": "Sriram Raghavan is an Indian film director and screenwriter who works in Hindi cinema. He is primarily considered an auteur of neo-noir action thrillers.\n\nRaghavan made his directorial debut with Ek Hasina Thi (2004). He then went on to direct the critically acclaimed Johnny Gaddaar (2007), an adaptation of the 1962 French novel Les mystifi\u00e9s by Alain Reynaud-Fourton. His prominence increased with Andhadhun (2018), which tells the story of a blind piano player who unwittingly becomes embroiled in the murder of a retired actor. The film received critical acclaim and was commercially successful. Raghavan is the recipient of several accolades, including two National film Awards and two Filmfare Awards.",
